=== the top level
top: BASHPID is $$
=== ( ) and $( )
paren: own BASHPID
cmdsub: own BASHPID
nested: own BASHPID
pipe: own BASHPID
=== each subshell has a different value
sequential substitutions differ
outer and inner differ
=== the value is an integer and $$ stays the same
integer
$$ unchanged in $( )
=== it is restored when the subshell ends
restored
=== an EXIT trap in a subshell sees the subshell's value
same value in the trap
=== per-subshell temp names do not collide
2
